      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(1A) To avoid doubt, the obligations imposed by subsection (1) do not\nlimit and are not limited by any other obligations imposed, or\nrights conferred, by this section.\n\n(1AB) If a representative of an Aboriginal legal assistance organisation is\nnotified under subsection (1), the investigating official must not\nquestion the person until the earlier of the following times:\n\nObligations of investigating officials  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 75, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2018\n\n(a) the representative has communicated with the person;\n\n(b) 2 hours have elapsed since the representative was notified.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(1A) To avoid doubt, the obligations imposed by subsection (1) do not\nlimit and are not limited by any other obligations imposed, or\nrights conferred, by this section.\n\n(1AB) If a representative of an Aboriginal legal assistance organisation is\nnotified under subsection (1), the investigating official must not\nquestion the person until the earlier of the following times:\n\nObligations of investigating officials  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 75, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2018\n\n(a) the representative has communicated with the person;\n\n(b) 2 hours have elapsed since the representative was notified.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-2-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-2-sec-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6bbf17a0106ba186601407b1fb58371299285fb2e6b6e78064bd7a9d830b8490",
      "skos:note": "Representatives of Aboriginal legal assistance organisations must not question people until notified."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-2-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 After subsection 23H(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(1A) To avoid doubt, the obligations imposed by subsection (1) do not\nlimit and are not limited by any other obligations imposed, or\nrights conferred, by this section.\n\n(1AB) If a representative of an Aboriginal legal assistance organisation is\nnotified under subsection (1), the investigating official must not\nquestion the person until the earlier of the following times:\n\nObligations of investigating officials  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 75, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2018\n\n(a) the representative has communicated with the person;\n\n(b) 2 hours have elapsed since the representative was notified."
    },
