    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-3-sec-2-ss-1b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2(1B) Subsection 15HK(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-3-sec-2-ss-1b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(e) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the disclosure will endanger the health or safety of any\nperson or prejudice the effective conduct of a controlled\noperation.\n\nControlled operation disclosure offence  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 75, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2018\n\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraphs (1B)(b) and (d) and\nsubparagraph (1B)(e)(ii)—see section 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(1B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(e) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the disclosure will endanger the health or safety of any\nperson or prejudice the effective conduct of a controlled\noperation.\n\nControlled operation disclosure offence  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 75, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2018\n\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraphs (1B)(b) and (d) and\nsubparagraph (1B)(e)(ii)—see section 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-3-sec-2"
      },
