        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1E) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses information; and\n\n(b) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(c) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the person knows that the disclosure will endanger the\nhealth or safety of any person or prejudice the effective\nconduct of a controlled operation.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraph (1E)(b)—see\nsection 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(1E) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses information; and\n\n(b) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(c) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the person knows that the disclosure will endanger the\nhealth or safety of any person or prejudice the effective\nconduct of a controlled operation.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraph (1E)(b)—see\nsection 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-3-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-3-sec-2-ss-1e-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-3-sec-2-ss-1e-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80906c8647639d9f82b3e84d16e8e7afb2b81969483636679e1e75c3335e1933",
      "skos:note": "Disclosing information about a controlled operation can be an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-3-sec-2-ss-1e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2(1E) Subsection 15HK(1)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1E) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses information; and\n\n(b) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(c) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the person knows that the disclosure will endanger the\nhealth or safety of any person or prejudice the effective\nconduct of a controlled operation.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraph (1E)(b)—see\nsection 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years."
    },
