        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-7-sec-86c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "purpose\n\nA target entity may collect for an integrity purpose sensitive\ninformation that:\n\n(a) if the target entity is a Privacy Act agency—is reasonably\nnecessary for, or directly related to, one or more of the\nentity’s functions or activities; or\n\n(b) if the target entity is a wholly-owned Commonwealth\ncompany—is reasonably necessary for one or more of the\nentity’s functions or activities.\nNote:\nSubclause 3.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 3 limits the\ncircumstances in which an APP entity may collect sensitive\ninformation. This section lets a target entity collect sensitive\ninformation for an integrity purpose in circumstances corresponding to\nthose in which it may collect other personal information (see\nsubclauses 3.1 and 3.2 of that Principle).",
      "skos:definition": "purpose\n\nA target entity may collect for an integrity purpose sensitive\ninformation that:\n\n(a) if the target entity is a Privacy Act agency—is reasonably\nnecessary for, or directly related to, one or more of the\nentity’s functions or activities; or\n\n(b) if the target entity is a wholly-owned Commonwealth\ncompany—is reasonably necessary for one or more of the\nentity’s functions or activities.\nNote:\nSubclause 3.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 3 limits the\ncircumstances in which an APP entity may collect sensitive\ninformation. This section lets a target entity collect sensitive\ninformation for an integrity purpose in circumstances corresponding to\nthose in which it may collect other personal information (see\nsubclauses 3.1 and 3.2 of that Principle).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-7-sec-86c-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7e45b08db42055a0a8dcd11af54794f67f34d75510d055c1f77201ecaa360adb",
      "skos:note": "Target entity may collect sensitive information for integrity purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-7-sec-86c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "86C Target entity may collect sensitive information for integrity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "purpose\n\nA target entity may collect for an integrity purpose sensitive\ninformation that:\n\n(a) if the target entity is a Privacy Act agency—is reasonably\nnecessary for, or directly related to, one or more of the\nentity’s functions or activities; or\n\n(b) if the target entity is a wholly-owned Commonwealth\ncompany—is reasonably necessary for one or more of the\nentity’s functions or activities.\nNote:\nSubclause 3.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 3 limits the\ncircumstances in which an APP entity may collect sensitive\ninformation. This section lets a target entity collect sensitive\ninformation for an integrity purpose in circumstances corresponding to\nthose in which it may collect other personal information (see\nsubclauses 3.1 and 3.2 of that Principle)."
    },
